@There are many locks in sam9407 driver:

-- queue locks:

  Driver is designed to use four independent queues. The purpose of these
queues is to wait for command acknowledges or status data, returned thru
interrupt dispatch.
  When queue is non-NULL (this means that command is expecting some data to
be returned thru interrupt), queue is spin_locked in queue->lock and status
bits are set in status field. We wait for ACK interrupt and then eventually
for interrupts which carry return message. Status bits are set to reflect
what we expect to be returned after command is sent.
  When queue is busy, we spin-wait for queue on queue->lock to be released.
Queue lock is released when all data is received (or command data receive
timeout happens). Status bits are set in interrupt handler, and communication
with wait loop is handled thru atomic bitops.
  When queue is NULL, no interrupts are expected on command and no queue
locking is performed. This way, on NULL queue commands can be sent with
disabled interrupts.

-- command lock:
  
  Commands on locked and non-locked queues are serialized by sam->command_lock
spinlock. This spinlock should disable interrupts, because we can send command
from async (audio, MIDI receive) interrupt handler. Otherwise, sending command
bytes to hardware is synchronized by busy-waiting on RF hardware status bit.

  We do not need to lock HW status reads, as they are atomic to us. All returned
data is delivered by interrupt. Returned data is processed by interrupt handler
and dispatched to (already locked) queues. Synchronous data returned on unlocked
queue indicates error condition.

-- memory transfer lock:

  Memory transfers are serialized by hardware transfer lock. Before transfer,
we should acquire internal hardware lock (indicated thru ACK/NAK on WRT_MEM
and RD_MEM commands)

-- MMT (memory management table) lock:

  Serializes access to MMT updating. MMT is shadowed in memory and it is
locked in sam->mmt_lock spinlock. This lock protects MMT table and mmt address
fields. It is exclusive locked, because MMT is usually read-modified-wrote on
MMT entry alloc/free. Memory management routines should not be called with
disabled interrupts, because they expect ACK/NAK to be returned, so MMT lock
should not block interrupts.

-- CTL (control table shadow) lock:

  Serializer access to control table shadow. As this table is mostly read,
lock is realized as rw_lock spinlock. It allows concurent readers, but only
one writer at a time. In hope that control element operators are not called
from interrupts, this spinlock is not interrupt blocking.

-- open lock

  Serializes access to voice allocation. IRQ blocking, because voice can be
acquired/released from interrupt context.@


